  "body": "[4.13.1.2 Creating a customized built-in element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#custom-elements-customized-builtin-example) says:\r\n\r\n    const plasticButton2 = new PlasticButton();\r\n    console.log(plasticButton2.localName);          // will output \"button\"\r\n    console.log(plasticButton2.getAttribute(\"is\")); // will output \"plastic-button\"\r\n\r\nHowever, I couldn't find a step to add ```is``` attribute in ```new``` case though I found [it in document.createElement() case](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-document-createelement)\r\n",
